Build-host paths
----------------

`libksud.so` embeds a build-user cargo-registry path (`…/.cargo/registry/…`)
from the machine that built it. The binary is otherwise unmodified from the
repository artifact. Rebuild with `RUSTFLAGS="--remap-path-prefix=$HOME=/build"`
to strip such paths in future refreshes.

LKM (`dfroot.ko`)
-----------------

The LKM binary is intentionally NOT committed. It is built from
`lkm/dfroot.c` (GPL-2.0-only, `MODULE_LICENSE("GPL")`) by the top-level
`Makefile` (one podman build for the single KMI `android13-5.15`, using the
digest-pinned image
`ghcr.io/ylarod/ddk-min:android13-5.15-20260828@sha256:9e68cd9fcab748584755d31ba88ef134efc938dbde17f258c2652315f6cd81cd`
resolved via `scripts/ddk-image.sh`) or by CI
(`.github/workflows/build.yml`), and copied to
`app/src/main/jni/ko/dfroot-android13-5.15.ko` (all `*.ko` under that directory
are gitignored). CI strips `.note.gnu.build-id`, so the CI/release artifact
(13,384 B, sha256
`9dfb8b71b306f5a38fd8b35b283d4dab8b4eb25a08ad97ca0f4ef705b6151c68`) is not
byte-identical to the local `make` build (13,504 B, sha256 `94f8be98…`, which
retains the build-id note). Fresh clones must run the LKM build
(or download CI artifacts) before `assembleRelease`; see README.md and
PORTING-GZIF.md §8.

